The classes $b_0,b_1$ are fixed by the page monodromy, and $$\label{eq:arith-boundary-pairings}
 \begin{aligned}
 e(b_j,b_j)&=-\frac{n_j^2}{4},&
 e(b_0,b_1)&=-\frac14,\\
 4e(b_j,x)&\equiv-\tau(x)\pmod4&&(x\in E).
 \end{aligned}$$

The quadratic form $B_
u|F_{
u,1}$ is indefinite and has dimension at least five. The Hermitian form on $F_{
u,5}$ has dimension at least two over $L$ and is indefinite at the real place of $L^+$ indexed by the pair $\{\zeta, ar\zeta\}$. Both assertions hold for $
u=0,1$.

